    "1": {
      "note": "<strong>gau3 meng6</strong> (救命, literally 'save life') is the universal cry for help. Hong Kong's emergency number is <strong>999</strong>, which connects to police, fire, and ambulance. <em>gap1 zing3 sat1</em> (急症室) is the A&E department; <em>gau3 wu6 ce1</em> (救護車) is the ambulance, literally 'save-protect car'. Note <strong>zau2</strong> (走) — context matters: in everyday speech it means 'leave/go', but in emergencies it means 'flee/run away'.",
